-- title:
--   Regular special fibre at an ordinary point, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ not divisible by $q$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, together with a ring embedding $L\hookrightarrow\mathbb{C}$ carrying $\zeta$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $X_H$ function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of the unit-group reduction map for `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, and with $K$ an $A$-algebra over $L$. Let $j\in K$, nonzero, have Laurent expansion the coefficient-embedded $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $W_0$ be the valuation subring of $K$ consisting of the $f$ of the form $x/y$ with $x,y$ power series over $A$ and $y$ of nonzero reduction. On the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) (the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$), let $z$ be a point, $\varpi_z$ the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under `toBase`, assumed to lie in the maximal ideal of the stalk; let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}$ of the finite chart algebra $A_{\mathrm{fin}}=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` map to $z$, with $y$ maximal, and assume every $b\in A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ lying in the nonunits of $W_0$ lies in $y$. Let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\varphi:A_{\mathrm{fin}}\to\Omega$ a ring homomorphism with kernel $y$ such that $\varphi(j)$ is not in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants all of whose elliptic models have no nonzero $q$-torsion point. Let $K_0\le K$ be the base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, an $A$-algebra over $L$, with $j_0\in K_0$ nonzero of the same Laurent expansion, let $\iota:$ `chartAlgFin A K₀ j₀` $\to A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the inclusion $K_0\subseteq K$, and assume the floor model `toBase A K₀ j₀` is smooth. Then, viewing $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ as an algebra over the floor chart algebra via $\iota$: if $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ is unramified over the floor chart algebra at every prime $\mathfrak Q\subseteq y$ of height $1$, the quotient of the stalk of $\mathfrak X$ at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is a purity statement for the normalised full-level integral model: regularity of the special fibre at a closed ordinary point is deduced from unramifiedness over a smooth $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor at the height-one primes below that point. It is the $q=3$ case, matching the statement for $q\ge 5$, and feeds the regularity statement for the two-chart model over a perfect residue field.
